statement.raw_tex:
\begin{Thm}\label{Thm:5-4}
  Suppose GPA generates an infinite sequence of iteration points $\{\xv_c\}$ that converges to a critical point $\xv_*$. Then, we have the following estimations on convergence rate.
  \begin{itemize}
    \item If $\theta=1/2$, there exist $\gamma>0$ and $\mu\in(0,1)$ such that
      \begin{equation*}
        \|\xv_c-\xv_*\| \le \gamma\mu^c.
      \end{equation*}
    \item If $\theta\in(1/2,1)$, there exist $\gamma_1>0$ and $\gamma_2>0$ such that
      \begin{equation*}
        |f(\xv_c)-f(\xv_*)| \le \gamma_1 c^{-\frac{1}{2\theta-1}} \qquad\text{ and }\qquad
        \|\xv_c-\xv_*\| \le \gamma_2 c^{-\frac{1-\theta}{2\theta-1}}.
      \end{equation*}
  \end{itemize}
\end{Thm}

